  "body": "## What this adds\n\nThis adds a single file, `docs/research/p104-side-correction-scope-map.md`. It is a navigation map for the revision-4 `p104-side-correction` card, in the style of `docs/research/complex-decoder-scope-map.md`. No new mathematics, no review dispositions, no \u03ba or selected-frontier change.\n\nFourteen PRs and threads now work on the same `I-G/2` completion of the native P104 channel, many from the last two hours. The map pins each to its exact head and records three things: which premise it fixes (cut, transports kept, storage, frame paths, producer, precision), what it concludes, and what it explicitly leaves outside.\n\nSources covered:\n- open PRs https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2082, https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2083, https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2089, https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2090, https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2096, https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2113 and https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2127;\n- the channel in https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1972 and https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1991;\n- discussions https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2080, https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2092, https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2107, https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2121 and https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2131.\n\nIt follows revision 4's request to \"summarize which common premise has been tested and what the next search would change\".\n\n## The one derived observation\n\nCrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#2082 and CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#2083 price completions under the same conditional coverage contract (s = N = 9, m = 73, W = 832, unchanged idle requirements). Under it, a correction with no creditable progress keeps the zero-saving moment at or below one only if it adds at most **328/9 \u2248 36.4 rank units per call**. CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#2082 states the same slack. Every route covered so far is either infeasible (the 8-array cuts) or needs at least 96 added transports. The constructions and candidates pay 208.\n\nSo within the shared premises the route is closed. Only two kinds of change remain open:\n1. replacing or fusing original transports, or adding new frame paths (live claims in https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2121 and https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2131);\n2. a coverage interface that credits added transports.\n\nThe map also notes that closing the 96..208 gap doesn't matter under the retained contract.\n\n## Checks\n\n- The doc's Python snippet reproduces the cited moments exactly with `fractions`: 7659/7592 at 96, 1917/1898 at 104, 7785/7592 at 208, 7551/7592 uncorrected, and the 328/9 slack. Constants are taken from the PR bodies, not from fresh package replays.\n- Both relative links resolve. There are no bare PR references.\n- `python3.12 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_research_*.py'`: 65 tests OK (3 skipped).\n- All nine PR heads were re-checked unchanged at 20:25 UTC. Canonical main is still `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2` (priority revision 4).\n- The overlap refresh (389 open PRs, 796 discussion records, complete pagination) found no other scope map. One P104 claim appeared at 20:17 UTC (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/2131) and is included.\n\n**Not checked:** I did not replay any cited package, so the open-PR entries are their authors' claims as stated. The map is a dated snapshot and will go stale as these PRs change; each entry gives its head for that reason.\n\n## Task\n\n- Drawn: complex-mechanisms, card `p104-side-correction`, chooser nonce `babf7d7d03bf6b191d708ecb1d52d2aa`, base `0fdd7d82`.\n- Scope **changed** to consolidation, because every concrete sub-question was already claimed or in an open PR.\n- Claim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18933452.\n\n## Credit\n\nAll results belong to their authors: Rohan Arun, Chafik Boukhalfa, Adam Gall, David Arias, Jeremy Diviney, Ross Richardson, 1337isnot1337, Jose Manuel and the credited lineage. The coverage contract sources are Dominik Scholz's paired-chain model, Sagar Thakrar (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1012) and Douglas Colkitt (https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1240). Authors: corrections to how I summarized your scope are welcome.\n\nPrepared by Aaron Wang / navinor, with help from Claude Code. Apache-2.0. Not requesting merge; selected frontier unchanged.\n",
